cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "MB-CFD: prescribed-wall moving-boundary CFD for patient-specific aortic hemodynamics (svMultiPhysics)"
authors:
  - family-names: Halter
    given-names: Elie
    email: elie.halter@gmail.com
  - family-names: Colombo
    given-names: Monika
    affiliation: "Aarhus University, Department of Mechanical and Production Engineering"
abstract: >-
  Open-source pipeline (svMultiPhysics + SimVascular/TetGen) for moving-boundary versus
  rigid-wall CFD of the patient-specific thoracic aorta. The MRI-derived wall motion is
  imposed on the wall, faded to zero over 12 mm next to the fixed caps, and the interior
  mesh is moved by the solver's mesh equation; a patch makes the fluid assembly
  consistent with the discrete geometric conservation law. Tools for re-timing the wall
  motion, removing its rigid-body part, building rigid references at any cardiac phase
  and computing volume-weighted lumen means are included.
keywords:
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - moving boundary
  - arbitrary Lagrangian-Eulerian
  - aortic hemodynamics
  - 4D-flow MRI
  - mesh morphing
license: MIT
